# DEC-260, batch 4 of 4: the member-facing English still written inline in 35 of Civicsmith's modules, keyed (Bob
# through BOB, K3366: a module reads its words by key through setup-words' word(key, vars) and holds no English;
# DEC-258's model). The modules: calculations, standards, action-plans, monitoring, connections, run-rules, reading-
# pipeline, investigation, calc-grammar, progressions, capture-requests, people, provenance, credentials, local-facts,
# bias, reading-guides, actions, sources, connection-grammar, docket, query.mjs, render.mjs, question-explorer, notice-
# producers, calibration, attestation, project-stage, action-holds, extractrun.mjs, accepted-work, contradiction.mjs,
# host-governor, signin-door, tokens.mjs. What it keys: refusal translations by their code (refusal.<CODE>; where a code
# is already keyed, the design's words govern), including question-explorer's exploring-run refusals; the why, basis and
# says lines a member reads in answers (calculations' and calc-grammar's undetermined reasons, standards' force and
# period reasons, connections' on-point and timing reasons, reading-pipeline's OCR and AI transcription notes, run-
# rules' run endings, bounds and bars, people's identity grades, bias lenses and debts, render's capture completeness),
# notice and queue texts (notice-producers, monitoring's tick reasons, capture-requests' waits), document texts members
# read (a standard's source section, project-stage's stage reasons) and labels, as <module>.<slug> or
# <module>.<why|says|note|label|blurb|summary>.<slug>; a text an existing key already says reads that key. Spelling is
# American, internal codes are dropped from member text, template variables are {name}. Left in source, each with its
# reason in words-reads-mod-4.json: refusal details, wire grammar and field descriptions, act names inside gate details,
# diagnostics, method tags, the project file's own log grammar, the deployment order's constants, and prompts the
# assistant reads. Run: python3 words-mod-4.src.py, then node build_words.mjs.
import json, os
W = []
def w(key, en, prot=False, note=''):
    W.append(dict(key=key, en=en, protected=prot, note='DEC-260' + (': ' + note if note else '')))

