w("refusal.ADOPTION_NO_EDITION", "An adoption names the edition adopted, as it is written, in at most 50 characters. None was given. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_ASK_BOUND_ABOVE_CEILING", "Nothing was asked, because the question was given more room than one question may have — more turns, more reading or more time than the most allowed. Ask again within those limits.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_BAD_EXPIRY", "An agent credential lasts a whole number of days, from 1 to 365, and 90 if you do not say. That was not one of them. Nothing was created. Choose a number of days, or leave it out.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_IDENTITY_TAKEN", "That name already belongs to an agent credential in your team's Civicsmith. Acts in the record cite the name, so binding it to something new would quietly change who did work that has already been done. Retire the old one or choose another name.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_MINT_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Only a named person signed in to your team's Civicsmith can create an agent credential. Deciding what an automated worker is allowed to reach is a judgment somebody has to be accountable for, so an automated worker cannot make it — not even about itself.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_NO_SECRET", "The agent credential could not be created, because your team's Civicsmith was not handed the fingerprint of its secret, and a credential without one could never be used. Nothing was created. Try again; if it keeps happening, tell whoever hosts your team's Civicsmith.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_PRINCIPAL_NOT_THE_MINTER", "A credential that acts for one member acts for the member who creates it, and nobody else. You named another member, and nobody can authorize an agent in someone else's name: it would see what they see and its work would be recorded as theirs. Nothing was created. The member it should act for can create it themselves.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_PRINCIPAL_UNSTATED", "An agent credential has to say who stands behind it: the organization as a whole, or one named member. The two carry different accountability and they see different things, so the record will not hold one that says neither.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_REVOKE_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Withdrawing an agent credential is recorded against the person who withdrew it, so a named member has to be the one doing it. An automated caller has no name to put there and the record would then show a decision nobody made.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_CREDENTIAL_UNKNOWN", "There is no agent credential by that name in your team's Civicsmith, so nothing was withdrawn. Being told that plainly matters more than it looks: believing you have taken an authority away when you have not is the worse of the two outcomes.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_GROUP_TEST_INVALID", "This test investigation was not added, because it does not say all it must: which part of the assistant it tests, the matter itself, and the answers people wrote for it. Your team's own tests show how the assistant does on your matters; they never switch a part on or off.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_NO_ACCOUNT", "Nothing was run, because no account serves your request: you have not connected a Claude account or an API key of your own, and your team has no API key of its own switched on, or the account that would serve has this use switched off. Connect yours, or ask an administrator about the team's.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_PART_NOT_DEPLOYED", "This part of the assistant has not yet passed Civicsmith's tests, so it is not switched on in your team's Civicsmith. Everything else works without it.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUNS_NO_CONTEXT_ID", "That request named a kind of thing but not which one. Background work belongs to a particular question or a particular project, and the record answers for the one you are looking at rather than for all of them.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUNS_NO_CONTEXT_TYPE", "That request did not say what kind of thing to look in. Background work is attached either to a question or to a project, and those are different places — so the record asks which rather than choosing one for you.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUNS_UNKNOWN_CONTEXT_TYPE", "Background work is not attached to anything of that kind. Rather than answer as though nothing were running there, the record says so and names the kinds of thing it does attach work to.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_ALREADY_OPEN", "Nothing was run, because a run with this name is already on record here. The record keeps what each run did under its own name, so starting a second one under a name already in use would write two different histories into one place. Give this one a name of its own.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_BOUND_PLANE_COUNTED", "This part of the investigation's budget is kept by the record itself — passages marked citable, questions opened and pages read are counted as the work lands, and whether the investigation is still alive is read off the clock — so the investigation cannot report it, up or down. Nothing was recorded for this step.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_BOUND_UNKNOWN", "The investigation named a part of its budget that does not exist, or did not say which part it meant. Nothing was recorded, so no budget was spent or set that nobody could account for.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_BOUND_UNNAMED", "The run stopped without saying what stopped it. Not finding something and not finishing the search are different facts, and only one of them licenses a conclusion.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE", "Nothing was run, because your team's Civicsmith could not find an account to run it under. That is a fact about our setup and not an answer about your question: no searching happened, so nothing here should be read as having looked and found nothing.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_CONSUME_INVALID", "The investigation gave an amount for its budget that is not a whole number of zero or more. A budget is set and used up in whole steps, and never goes down, so nothing was recorded for this step.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_EXPLORE_NEEDS_STEP", "Nothing was started, because exploring a question unasked is always done as one step of the work, and this did not say which step. The step is what records why it ran and what it found.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_EXPLORE_NOT_DEPLOYABLE", "Nothing was started, because exploring a question unasked is switched on only after investigating has been checked in real use and has passed its test investigations.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_MODE_NOT_DEPLOYED", "Nothing was run, because the kind of work this run asked for is not switched on for your team's Civicsmith yet. Kinds of work are switched on one at a time, each only after the one before it has been checked in real use. Ask for a kind that is switched on, or leave the kind out to run the one that is.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_MODE_UNCHECKED", "Nothing was run, because this kind of work has nothing in place yet to check what it is asked to work on. Rather than start without that check, the run is refused until the part that provides it is running.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_NOT_A_MEMBER_ACT", "Nothing was started, because the assistant starts work only when a member asks for it. The one exception is a standing question a member wrote themselves, which may only read and only answer that question. Nothing here asked on a member's behalf, so nothing ran.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_NOT_PROJECT_MEMBER", "Asking the system to look into a project is work inside that project, and this account is not one of that project's participants. This is not about what the account is allowed to do in general — it is about which piece of work it is part of. Someone who owns that project can invite you to it.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_NO_CONTEXT", "Nothing was run, because the request did not say what the run is for or what it belongs to. A run has to sit inside a question or a project so that the people working on that question can see it happened; one belonging to nothing would be invisible to everybody.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_NO_SUCH_CONTEXT", "Nothing of the kind this run names answers to that id here. A run is over a question or a project, nothing else; a run over a question has to name a question, and a run over a project has to name a project. Something you cannot see is answered exactly as something that does not exist, so this says nothing about whether anything else goes by that id.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_PLAN_NEEDS_MEMBER", "Nothing was run, because a planning run is started only by a member of the team, for one plan at a time. Nothing starts one by itself, so a request that has no member behind it cannot start one.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_PLAN_NEEDS_PROJECT", "Nothing was run, because a planning run was asked for outside a project. A plan belongs to the project whose members will decide what to do, so a planning run is started from inside that project.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_PLAN_NO_SEARCH", "Nothing was run, because this planning run was allowed to fetch new material or to start further searches. A planning run proposes options from what the record already holds and does not go looking, so those parts of its budget are left out.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_PLAN_REQUIRED", "Nothing was run, because a planning run was asked for without saying which plan it is for. A planning run works on one plan at a time, so it names that plan before it starts.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_PLAN_UNEXPECTED", "Nothing was run, because this run named a plan but is not a planning run. Only a planning run works on a plan, so any other run is started without one and its record does not suggest otherwise.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_READ_NO_AI", "Nothing was read, because this document is kept away from the assistant by a limit your team put on its material. The investigation goes on without it; a person can still read it.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_RERUN_OTHER_CONTEXT", "Nothing was run, because the earlier run it says it repeats belongs to a different question or project. Repeating work means asking the same question again under the lens that is in force for it — somewhere else the team's declared lens can be a different one, so the two runs would not be comparable and settling anything on that basis would be wrong.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_RERUN_SELF", "Nothing was run, because this run was told it is a re-run of itself. A re-run says which EARLIER piece of work it repeats, and a run pointing at itself would be able to clear its own outstanding re-run. Name the earlier run, or leave the field out.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_RERUN_UNKNOWN", "Nothing was run, because the earlier run it says it repeats is not one this record holds for you. It may never have existed, it may have been removed, or it may belong to work you have not been brought into. Check the name.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_SKILL_VERSION_UNNAMED", "This run did not say which version of its instructions it was working under. What a run found can only be read against the instructions it was given, so the record asks for that version before the run starts rather than guessing at it afterward.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_STATE_TOO_LARGE", "The investigation tried to keep more working notes than one investigation may hold, so nothing it sent with them was recorded and none of its budget was spent. An investigation keeps a short list of what it has left to do, not everything it has read.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_STEP_UNKNOWN", "Nothing was started, because the step this investigation names is not one the record holds here. Something you cannot see is answered exactly as something that does not exist.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_RUN_VERIFICATION_UNFIT", "This record of a kind of work checked in real use was not kept, because it does not say all it must: which kind of work, which run was checked, which person checked it, and what they saw. A machine cannot record that its own work was checked. Until such a record is kept, the next kind of work stays switched off.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.AI_TEST_BAR_UNFIT", "This result on the test investigations was not kept, because it does not say all it must: which part of the assistant was tested, on which set and which version of it, how often it raised a false alarm, whether it passed, who graded it and when. Until such a result is kept, that part stays switched off.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ARRIVAL_BAD", "An arrival names the source that brought it and when, as an instant. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_DISCLOSURE", "A disclosure names what was revealed (a pseudonym link, an attribute or a name), how it became known, and to whom it is known, each from the listed choices. The field that is not one of them is named. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_FREQUENCY", "That is not a frequency this record knows. Choose one of the listed frequencies, or none to return the address to the frequency its documents set. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_KEY", "That is not a public key this team can register. It takes the base64 part of an ssh-ed25519 public key, the part that begins AAAA. Nothing was written.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_REASON", "The reason is too long or contains a quotation mark, a backslash or a line break, which the record cannot keep as written. Shorten it to one plain line. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_REQUIRED", "One step does not say how firmly it is expected, in one of the five words the record understands (always, usually, sometimes, never, unless an exception is recorded). Use one of them. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BAD_STAGE", "The step named here is not a step of this flow as it is declared now. Name one of its steps. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_ADOPTION_NOT_AUTHORED", "Adopting a bias set is an authored, attributed act and an automated credential has no name to put on it. Sign in as a member.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_ADOPTION_NOT_PROPOSED", "That bias set has not been proposed for adoption, so there is nothing to adopt yet. A set is written, then proposed, then adopted — and the middle step is what stops a set becoming binding without anybody having offered it.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_ADOPTION_NO_REASON", "Nothing was adopted, because no reason was given. Adopting a lens changes how this team reads evidence, so the record keeps, beside your name, why you are adopting it. Say why in a sentence or a short paragraph (at most 2,000 characters) and adopt it again.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_ALREADY_SETTLED", "Nothing was added, because this one has already been settled — by the lens moving back, by a re-run under the lens now in force, or by a member who gave their reason. What settled it is on the record and is not overwritten. If the lens changes again, the obligation is raised again as a new one.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_MACHINE_CANNOT_RESOLVE", "Nothing was settled. This was asked by a machine credential, and saying that a lens change does not affect a finding is a person's judgment about the work — not something an automated account can decide on anyone's behalf. A machine may raise this and show it to you; answering it is yours.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_NO_ACTOR", "Nothing was settled, because this request has no member behind it. Deciding that a change in the team's declared lens does not affect a piece of work is somebody's judgment, and the record keeps whose it was. Sign in and do it as yourself.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_NO_REASON", "Nothing was settled, because no reason was given. The whole of what this act puts on the record is why you judged that the change in the lens does not bear on this work — without it the record would say only that somebody decided, and a later reader could not tell whether the question was answered or waved away. Say why, and it is settled.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_NO_RUN", "Nothing was settled, because the request did not say which piece of work it is about. A bias debt belongs to one assistant run — the one whose lens changed — so settling it has to name that run.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_NO_SUCH_DEBT", "Nothing was settled, because there is no open bias debt on that run here. Either the run never carried one, or it has already been settled, or it is not a run you can open.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_DEBT_REASON_TOO_LONG", "Nothing was settled, because the reason given is longer than this record holds for one. Nothing about it was wrong — it is a size limit and not a judgment about what you wrote. Put the reasoning where it belongs in the work and give the short form of it here.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_INHALE_CANNOT_ADOPT", "Reading a policy proposes a bias set; it never adopts one. Adopting is something a member does with their name on it, because otherwise a team could say it follows an organization's standards without anybody in the team having agreed to anything.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_PATTERN_UNCITED", "A pattern statement is a claim about how an institution actually behaves, so it is analysis and needs evidence in the record. It can be written in draft without one; it cannot leave draft without one.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_REFUSED", "That bias set was not written. One or more of its statements is not something the record can honor, and each one is named below with what is wrong with it. Nothing was saved, so nothing needs undoing — correct the statements and write it again.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_RESIDUE_UNSTATED", "This bias set is adopted and does not say what it does NOT check. A case held to a standard has to say which parts of that standard this system verifies and which it does not — the parts that can be counted are rarely the parts that protect, and enforcing only the countable half while staying silent would carry the authority of the whole policy without its substance.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_STATEMENT_ISSUES_A_VERDICT", "That statement assigns a truth value to a source wholesale, and declared bias may never issue verdicts. It may raise scrutiny, it may block an inference, and it may assert a pattern it can evidence. The construct that fights undeclared distortion is held to a higher standard than the distortion, so this is refused whoever declares it.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_STATEMENT_IS_A_BAR", "That is a standard of evidence — how strong support must be before you assert it — and a standard is a BAR rather than a lens. Declare it as your project's required strength, where it will actually refuse work that falls short. Filed here it would refuse nothing, because a declared bias is disclosed and never gates.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_STATEMENT_MALFORMED_SHAPE", "One of these bias statements is missing something the record needs to apply it: a stable name, one of the three kinds it can be, or the sentence itself. The three kinds are raising scrutiny on a source, blocking or licensing an inference, and asserting an evidenced pattern — a standard of evidence is not one of them; that is a bar.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_STATEMENT_NO_JUSTIFICATION", "That statement does not say why the lens is held. A declared bias the system honors is one its author justified; without that it is an unstated prior with a form around it.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BIAS_STATEMENT_SUBJECT_NOT_REGISTERED", "That statement names its subject in prose rather than pointing at the subject registry. Registry entries are what let the record notice when a project statement and a team statement are about the same thing — in prose, nothing can tell, and a collision that is quiet is the one this construct exists to prevent.", note="bias' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.BRANCH_UNKNOWN", "A phase starts after, or a judgment leads to, a phase of the same scenario, or a matter the plan is about. The one named is neither. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_CANNOT_REGRADE", "A new measurement cannot re-grade the documents already read by that engine, and that holds even when the new measurement is WORSE. What the record does instead is name exactly which transcriptions were graded under the old measurement, so a person can look at them and decide. Grades in this record are things people put their name to.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_NO_PROBE", "Nothing here was actually measured. A release note, a changelog, a model card or a new version number all tell you an engine CHANGED — none of them tells you how well it now reads a page, and that is the number the record grades against. Run the probe and record what it scored, including the inputs you gave it, so somebody else can disagree with you later.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_SHAPE", "This measurement is not readable as one. It has to name an engine, a version, a date, and the probe run that produced it — and the quality figure, where there is one, has to be on the same scale the rest of this record uses.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_SIGNAL_CLAIMS_MEASUREMENT", "This announcement carries a quality figure. Noticing that a vendor announced something is useful and the record keeps it — it brings the next check forward. But what they say about their own product is a claim, and a grade in this record rests on a measurement. The announcement cannot stand in for the check, and it cannot change a grade on its own.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_SIGNAL_SHAPE", "This announcement is not readable as one. It has to say which engine it is about and where you saw it, because it is somebody else's statement about their own product and the record keeps it attributed to them.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_SUBJECT_NO_PROBE", "To put an engine on the calibration schedule you have to say which probe will check it. Registering measures nothing yet, but a schedule with no stated way of measuring is a promise nobody could keep, or tell was kept.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_SUBJECT_UNNAMED", "To put an engine on the calibration schedule you have to say which engine. Registering it measures nothing yet — it only says what will be checked, and so it has to name it.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_UNATTRIBUTED", "This measurement does not say who ran it. A measurement is something somebody did, and a later reader who doubts the figure needs to know whose it is to ask for it to be run again.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_UNDATED", "A measurement has to carry the day it was taken. How good an engine is, is a fact about a particular day — without one, nothing can tell whether anybody has checked recently, and nothing can ever supersede it.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAL_UNNAMED", "A measurement has to say exactly what it measured — which engine, and which version of it. Services are retrained and re-released under the same name, so the name alone cannot tell a later reader whether the thing you measured is the thing that read their document.", note="calibration's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_ATTRIBUTION_ONE_PRINCIPAL", "This capture could not be recorded as belonging to anybody in particular, so it was not made. An act that names one party where two acted reads as though a person did something a machine did, or the other way round, and that is worse than a missing document.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_CONDUCT_HOST_HELD", "The site this would fetch from has asked us to slow down, or has refused us recently, and we are waiting the interval it named. The request is still queued and will be made when the wait is over — nothing has been lost and nothing needs re-asking.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_CONDUCT_NO_PURPOSE", "Every request your team's Civicsmith makes says what it is for, so a source can tell a first capture from a routine re-check and throttle one without blocking the other. This one names a purpose that is not one of the things it could truthfully be doing.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_CONDUCT_TICK_SPENT", "This round of fetching has already been to that site once. Requests are spread out rather than sent in a burst, so this one waits for the next round. It is still queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_CONDUCT_UA_ILLEGIBLE", "Your team's Civicsmith will not fetch without saying who is asking and how to reach whoever is running it. Being refused honestly is a fact that can be recorded; being admitted by disguise is a claim that could not be defended later.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_CONDUCT_UA_UNRECORDED", "This request asked to fetch as the member's own browser, and the record does not hold what that browser is. Presenting an agent nobody actually used would be inventing a client rather than speaking as one, so it asks rather than guessing.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_FETCH_FAILED", "Your team's Civicsmith tried to fetch the document and the fetch did not land, so nothing was captured. That says nothing about the document or the site beyond this one attempt, and it is recorded as a look that could not tell. The request is still queued and is tried again on a later round, until it expires.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_HELD_BY_ANOTHER_BUNDLE", "The record already holds this document, under another record. A document has one home in the record — the first record that registered it — and registering it again here would move it away from there. Nothing was written. Cite the record that holds it, or, if you found it at a new address, that sighting is already recorded as a corroboration of the one it holds.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_HELD_IN_PARTS", "The record lists this document, but keeps it in parts rather than as one file, and your team's Civicsmith has no record of fetching it itself. A timestamp is only requested for bytes your team's Civicsmith can vouch for, so none was requested. Nothing is missing: do not capture the document again. If your team's Civicsmith fetches it from its address, it can then be co-attested.", note="attestation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_PLATFORM_MARK_REFUSED", "This mark could not be made or withdrawn. Marking a site as a platform that asks for a login is a member's own act, and it names one site by its plain host name, such as www.example.org. Nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_ADDRESS_NOT_HELD", "The assistant may read anywhere while it searches, but it asks to capture only an address the record already holds: one a held document was captured from, or one a held document links to, exactly as written, its query and anchor included. This address is not one of them, so nothing was queued or fetched.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_ADDRESS_TOO_LONG", "This web address is longer than 2,048 characters, the most a capture request may carry. A longer one is refused whole, never cut, because a shortened address would name a different page. Nothing was queued or fetched.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_CARRIES_A_CAPTURE", "A request asks for a document; it never brings one. The fetch is performed by your team's Civicsmith itself so that where the bytes came from is something the record established rather than something it was told, and a provenance chain anybody could hand us is one anybody could invent.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_CO_ARCHIVE_MALFORMED", "The choice about a public archive copy reads co_archive: true (ask for one), false (ask for none), or nothing to let the team's setting decide. This request sent something else. Nothing was queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_CO_ARCHIVE_NOT_A_MEMBERS", "Whether a capture also asks a public archive to keep a copy is a member's choice, or else the team's setting. This request was not made by a member, so it cannot choose. Nothing was queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_LEAD_IS_THE_TARGET", "This names the same question twice — the one being worked, and the one the document supposedly bears on. Evidence for the question you are already working is just evidence for it, and flagging it as belonging somewhere else would put a note in front of you saying a document you just asked for is about something other than what you asked.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_LEAD_NOT_AN_INQUIRY", "This says the document bears on another question, but what it names is not a question. The whole point of noting a lead is that somebody working that question will be told about it, and there is nobody to tell if it does not name one.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_NOT_AN_INQUIRY", "A capture is requested under a question, and the thing named here is not one. The question is what the request is accountable to, and a fetch belonging to nothing is a fetch nobody can later account for.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_NOT_PUBLIC", "What was asked for is not a public web address. What an investigation session may reach is what anybody could reach by typing it into a browser, so an address that is not public on its face is not asked for at all.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_NOT_RETRYABLE", "This request cannot be asked again. Only a request the source itself turned away, under a question you can see, goes back into the queue; a request that is still waiting, was captured, has expired, or was refused for any other reason does not. Nothing was changed.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_NO_RUN", "This request did not name the piece of work asking for it, or named one that is not running here. Every fetch your team's Civicsmith makes on its own is traceable to a session somebody opened, because that opening is what authorizes it.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_NO_STEP", "This request names a step of work that is not one you can see here. A request made for a step is tied to it, so the step it names must be one its asker can see; one that does not exist answers the same. Nothing was queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_RENDER_MALFORMED", "This asked for the page as a visitor would see it in a form your team's Civicsmith does not recognize. It reads render: true, or nothing at all for the document as the site serves it, so a request for the rendered page is never quietly turned into a request for the page's empty frame. Nothing was queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_REQUEST_SITE_KIND_UNKNOWN", "This request described the site it asks for in a way your team's Civicsmith does not recognize. It reads site_kind: \"personal\" for a private person's own site, \"platform\" for a page on a platform that asks for a login, or nothing for an ordinary public page. Nothing was queued.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_SOURCE_REFUSED", "The site turned this request away: it asked for a login, a payment or a different browser, or refused for another reason it gave. Nothing was captured. A member who can see the question may supply what the site asked for and ask again.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CAPTURE_SWEEP_OUT_OF_SCOPE", "This request asked to be filed under a sweep, and that sweep does not take it: the sweep is not ratified, is held, or does not reach this address. Nothing was fetched or filed under it. A request filed under a sweep answers to what members ratified for that sweep, so it is never stretched to fit.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CATEGORY_UNKNOWN", "An option's category is one of: mitigation, legal, awareness, journalistic, grassroots, other. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CHECKPOINT_JUDGED", "That checkpoint has already been judged. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CHECKPOINT_NOT_DUE", "That checkpoint is not due yet: its phase has not started, or its days have not passed. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CHECKPOINT_REFUSED", "A judgment names a scenario of the plan, one of its phases that has a checkpoint, whether it was met or not met, and a note of up to 500 characters. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code; B411 E1: plain words")
w("refusal.CLAIM_BAD_SOURCE", "A claim is a quoted part of one of the interview's answers, or your own words. Quote it exactly as it stands. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CLAIM_NO_FIND_STEP", "A claim is found through its \"find the record\" step. Make that step first, then tie the record to it. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CLAIM_NO_TEXT", "Say what the public body is remembered to have said or done, in at most 2,000 characters. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CLOSE_BAD_REASON", "A project closes as resolved, superseded or abandoned. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CLOSE_NOTE_TOO_LONG", "A closing note on what the team would do differently is at most 4,000 characters. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_CHOICE_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Choosing which mention of a subject is the one on point for a connection is a member's own act, done in their name. A machine may point out the mentions a document holds, but deciding which one a connection rests on is a judgment a person signs for.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_CHOICE_NOT_A_MENTION", "The mention named is not one this document carries for that subject. The choice is among the places the record actually read the subject in this document, by the reference as the reading recorded it; a mention the record never read cannot be the one a connection rests on.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_CHOICE_NO_CONNECTION", "That request does not name a connection this record holds and you can see. A connection is named by the two documents it joins and the subject that joins them, and it exists once the record has derived it — choose after it appears among the document's connections.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_CHOICE_OCCURRENCE_UNNAMED", "That reference was read at more than one place in this document, and each place is its own mention. Say which one is on point — by the occurrence the record lists for it, or by the place as the record names it — and the choice will rest on that place alone.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_PAIR_MENTION_UNCHOSEN", "This document mentions the same subject in more than one place, and the record linked the two documents through the strongest-graded mention without anyone choosing which mention is the one on point. Because another mention bears on the part you cited, whether this connection reaches your citation is undetermined rather than yes or no. A citation of the document as a whole is answered today; a member may also choose which mention is the on-point one for this connection, and the answer then follows that choice.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_PAIR_NO_CONTENT", "This record holds no passage with that address, so there is no part of a document whose connections could be weighed. A content address is minted when a citation first points at a passage — if you expected one here, the citation that would have made it has not been written yet.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_PAIR_OUTSIDE_EXTENT", "This connection was established by a reference somewhere else in the document, not in the part you cited. A citation that points at a passage stands on what is IN that passage, so it cannot borrow a link the record found elsewhere in the same file. Cite the part where the reference actually appears, or cite the document as a whole and say so.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONNECTION_PAIR_UNPLACED", "The record knows which reference links these two documents but not where in either document it was read, so it cannot say whether that reference falls inside the part you cited. This is stated rather than assumed either way: the connection is real and its reach into your citation is undetermined until the document is read with positions.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CONSENT_NOT_STANDING", "That consent cannot be recorded: the detail it names is not in this source's history, or consent to a wider audience already stands. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.COPY_CLAIM_NOT_CITED", "What a copy says of itself is recorded with the passage of its text that says it. None was named, or it is not one of the standard's passages. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.COPY_UNKNOWN", "A captured copy is official, a codifier's, the copy in force, a draft, superseded, produced in answer to a records request, a vendor's model, or not known. This one names none of these. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DATE_REFUSED", "A regulated date is written year-month-day and names its basis: the statute, order or commitment that sets it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DEFINITION_MOVED", "The version of the declared flow this decision names is not the one standing now. Rather than file your decision against a description you did not read, the record keeps it out and asks you to look again: read the question against the version in force and decide again. The answer may well be the same one, and it will then be yours. Both versions are named beside this message, the earlier one still reads back in full, and nothing was recorded.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DISPOSITION_UNKNOWN", "A disposition is one of: open, chosen, declined, done, blocked. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_ALREADY_WITHDRAWN", "That edition is already withdrawn, and a withdrawal is never repeated or lifted. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_ENTRY_SETTLED", "That entry is already settled: placed in public, declined, listed as received, or taken back. A later entry says what changed. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_KIND_UNKNOWN", "The entry's kind is not one the docket takes, or does not fit who it is from: a response or a statement comes from the subject or someone granted standing, a reaction from anyone else, and an outcome from anyone. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NOTHING_SEALED", "An unsealing order names a part that no sealing order on this case's docket names. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NOT_ATTRIBUTED", "Every docket entry says who it is from: the case's subject, someone granted standing, or the source's name, in at most 200 characters. This one names nobody. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NOT_A_PARTICIPANT", "Only a joined participant of the case's project files to its docket. Nothing was filed.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NOT_THE_MANAGER", "Only an owner of the case's project manages its public docket. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NOT_THE_SUBJECT", "The entry says it is from the case's subject, and the one it names is not a subject of the edition named. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_ARCHIVE_COPY", "A reaction elsewhere links to an independent archive's copy, and this capture has none. Ask for the archive copy again, then place it. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_CAPTURE", "Every docket entry has a captured copy with its origin, and the capture named is not one this record holds with the address it came from. Capture it first. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_EDITION", "Every docket entry names the edition of the case it concerns, and the edition named is not one this case has published. Name a published edition. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_GROUP_SLUG", "Your team has no name recorded yet, and a docket entry is never anonymous. Record the team's name first. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_REASON", "Say, in your own words and at most 2,000 characters, why, and choose whether the entry is for the record, for the public docket, or both. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_STANDING", "The entry relies on a grant of standing that is not in force: it was never made on this case's docket, or it has ended. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_NO_SUMMARY", "A summary is one paragraph of at most 600 characters: a reaction elsewhere is shown with one in the team's own words, and an outcome is filed with one in yours. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_ORDER_UNREADABLE", "A court order is placed with what it orders (remove, redact, seal or unseal), the published editions it names, and, to redact, seal or unseal, the parts of the edition it names. This one does not say so. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_PRESSURE_MARKED", "This docket entry is already marked as a threat; a mark is never rewritten. Nothing was marked.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_SIGNATURE_REFUSED", "The signature is not a valid signature of this docket entry by one of your own registered signing keys, for the reason named. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_STALE", "Your team's Civicsmith holds no prepared docket entry from you with this fingerprint, it was prepared more than an hour ago, or the docket has moved since. Prepare it again and sign what it shows. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_TAKE_BACK_FINAL", "A take-back is never itself taken back. Place the entry again if it should stand. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_WARNING_NOT_ACKNOWLEDGED", "A public docket entry is permanent: a later entry can take it back but never unsay it, and posting it says you have read that. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_WITHDRAWAL_FINAL", "A withdrawal is never taken back. To stand behind the case again, publish a new edition. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCKET_WRONG_SHELF", "A reaction goes only under reactions elsewhere, and every other public entry only on the listed shelf. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DRIVE_TICK_EXPORT_BYTES_ARE_THE_SHELL", "The check of that Google Drive document did not run: the export address said it was sending a document and sent a web page instead. Your team's Civicsmith reads the bytes rather than the label, so the application page was recognized and not compared against the captured document — comparing it would report a change on every visit that nobody made.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DRIVE_TICK_EXPORT_IS_THE_SHELL", "The check of that Google Drive document did not run: the export address answered with a web page rather than a document, which is what Drive does when a file stops being shared with anyone who has the link. Nothing was compared and nothing about the record changed — what is known is that your team's Civicsmith could not see the document today.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUPLICATE_PLACEMENT", "The same document is placed at the same step twice in this request. Place it once. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUPLICATE_STAGE", "Two steps of this flow share one key, so a document placed at that key could belong to either. Give each step its own key. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_ACCEPT_INVALID", "A find is accepted by a member, as found, edited, or set aside for her own. Nothing was recorded.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_BEARING_INVALID", "A find is gauged as supporting the question, cutting against it, or unclear, with a short account of how. Nothing was offered.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_FIND_UNKNOWN", "The system can offer only a capture, a passage or a connection the record holds and the paying account may see. Nothing was offered.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_MUTE_IN_PROJECT", "You take part in a project drawing on this question, so a find is dismissed there, for the project. Nothing was recorded here.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_NO_RUN", "No exploring run by that name is open for this caller. Nothing was done.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_NO_SUCH_FIND", "No find by that name was offered to you. Nothing was recorded.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_PAGES_BOUND", "This exploring run has read as many pages as it may. It stopped where it was.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_PERSON_CAP_REACHED", "An exploring run looks at no more than 20 people. This one reached that number, so it stopped and its step was set aside.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_PERSON_NOT_TIED", "The system looks at a person only when a member has tied that person to the question. This look was not made, and the exploring goes on without it.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_READ_KEPT_AWAY", "This document is kept away from the assistant, so the system did not read it.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXPLORE_RUN_ENDED", "This exploring run has ended. Nothing was done.", note="question-explorer's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_ACT_REFUSED", "A member confirms, corrects or disputes a local fact; this act is none of the three. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_HOW_REFUSED", "Say how you checked, in at most 500 characters: the official page and its address, a call to the office, a visit. None was given, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_VALUE_REFUSED", "A correction gives the corrected value, in the form the profile holds that fact in, and its source in at most 500 characters. The value is missing or not of that form, or the source is missing or too long. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FAMILY_UNKNOWN", "The series named for this standard is not one your team's jurisdiction profiles list. Name a series they list, or none. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_ALREADY_CONFIRMED", "This provision already has a confirmed force, which the answer names. Withdraw it, with your reason, before recording another. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_NO_CITATION", "A provision's force is recorded with the provision's own words that state it: a passage of the standard's text. None was named. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_NO_CRITERIA", "A provision at someone's discretion names the passage stating the criteria for using it, or says that none are stated. Neither was given. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_NO_HOLDER", "A provision at someone's discretion names the office or body that holds the discretion, as an entity the record holds. None was named. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_SOURCE_INVALID", "Where a standard's force comes from is a delegation, a resolution, an oversight approval, a court order or a contract, with the passage of the instrument stating it. This is not that. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_TEXT_NOT_HELD", "The force of a provision is read from its own words, and this standard's text is not held. Hold its text first. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORCE_UNKNOWN", "A provision requires, recommends or allows; a policy's provision may also be required or at an office's discretion. This one names none of these for its kind. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FREQUENCY_NO_REASON", "A frequency is set with a reason: one of the listed reasons, or your own words of up to 2,000 characters. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GATHERING_REFUSED", "This was not saved: the list of things to gather that it carries is not written the way the record writes them, and a gathering request is shown to members as data, so it must stay within its grammar. The findings beside this say which requests and what is wrong with each. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GRANT_NOT_HELD", "This ask's permission to read has ended: it lasts a short while, and ends when you sign out. Ask again. Nothing was read.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GRANT_OP_REFUSED", "An answer to your question may only read the record through the reads an ask allows, and never change anything. This request was outside them. Nothing was read or changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_BASED_ON_UNKNOWN", "A guide may say which guide or proposal it is based on, and the one named is not a guide or proposal you can see. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_CARRIES_CONDUCT", "A reading guide says only what to look for in a document, and where. Each item opens with \"Look for\", \"Note whether\", \"Note where\", \"Check whether\", \"Check that\", \"Watch for\" or \"Compare\", and none tells the assistant what to do, names a tool or an action, or states a rule or a permission. A procedure guide may name the acts and duties of a route, but none of its items speaks to the assistant or tells it what to do. The item named does not keep to this. Reword it. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_ITEMS_REFUSED", "A reading guide holds from 1 to 50 items, each a short label (at most 80 characters), what to look for (at most 500 characters) and, if you like, where to look (at most 200 characters), as plain text. A procedure guide holds from 1 to 50 items, each a route (at most 500 characters), if you like the reply to expect (at most 500 characters), and the citation the route rests on (at most 200 characters). The items given are not of that form. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_MEMBER_ACT", "Writing, reviewing, offering, adopting or retiring a reading guide is a member's act. An assistant may propose a guide for a member to take up; it may not do any of these. Sign in as an active member. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_NOT_OFFERABLE", "Only a guide your team has approved can be offered to another team. Have it reviewed and approved first. Nothing was sent.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_NOT_REVIEWABLE", "Only a guide not yet your team's can be reviewed: one a member wrote for themselves, or one adopted from another team. This one is already your team's or has been retired. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_NO_GROUP_SLUG", "An offered guide is labeled with your team's short name, and none is recorded for this team, so nothing can be offered. Whoever runs your team's Civicsmith can set it. Nothing was sent.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_OFFER_UNREADABLE", "What was given is not a reading guide another team offered, or it was changed after it was offered. Ask the offering team to send it again. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_PROPOSAL_NOT_MACHINE", "A proposed guide is the assistant's work, kept apart for members to take up. A member writes a guide directly instead. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_READ_ONLY", "This reading guide comes with every copy of Civicsmith and is the same for every team, so no team can review, offer or retire it. Write your team's own guide for this kind instead, based on it if you like. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_REASON_MISSING", "Refusing or retiring a reading guide needs a reason, in at most 500 characters, so its author and the team can see why. None was given, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_RETIRED", "This reading guide has been retired. It stays readable, and nothing more can be done to it. Write a new guide based on it if it is still needed. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_RETIRE_NOT_APPROVER", "A guide that is its author's alone is retired by its author; a team's guide by a member who could approve it, that is, any active member other than its author. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_REVIEW_BY_AUTHOR", "A reading guide is reviewed by a member other than the one who wrote or adopted it. Ask another member to review it. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_RUN_MISSING", "A proposed guide names the assistant's run that proposed it, so members can see where it came from. None was named. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GUIDE_VERDICT_UNKNOWN", "A review either approves the guide, making it your team's, or refuses it, keeping it its author's. Say which. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_ALREADY_RELEASED", "That litigation hold is already released, and a release is stated once. Nothing was written. If the team is preserving again, place a new hold.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_FROM_REFUSED", "A hold can say what prompted it: a pressure mark, a pressure record, a court docket entry marked as legal pressure, or a counsel matter. What this named is not one you can see at the place the hold is placed, so nothing was written.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_PROJECTS_REFUSED", "Projects are named as a list of their ids, at most fifty different ones, and asking whether projects are held names at least one. The list given was not of that form, so it was refused and nothing was written.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_REFUSED", "A litigation hold is recorded as in place or released, with a reason of up to 500 characters and no quotation mark, backslash or line break. This one was not, so nothing was written.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_RELEASE_IS_ITS_OWN_ACT", "Releasing a litigation hold is its own act, recorded with its own reason, so that a release is never a side effect of placing one. This asked to release a hold through the act that places one, so nothing was written. Use the release act.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.IMPORTED_NOT_ACCEPTED", "This finding rests on another team's finding that this team has not accepted at that edition. Accept that edition first, or take the leg out. Nothing was written.", note="accepted-work's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INTERVIEW_BAD_ANSWERS", "An interview holds six answers, one for each of its questions, in your own words; leave a question blank if you have no answer, and answer at least one. Nothing was kept.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INTERVIEW_NOT_A_LEG", "An interview is a member's own account, which says where to look and is never what a finding rests on. Rest the finding on what was found in the record. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INVESTIGATION_MEMBER_ONLY", "Only a member does this, in their own words and by their own choice. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INVESTIGATION_NO_REASON", "Say why, in your own words, in at most 2,000 characters. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.KEYED_SERVICE_NO_KEY", "No key was given for the service, so there is nothing to hold. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.KEYED_SERVICE_OFF", "The team's key for this outside service is switched off, or no key is held, so it was not used. Everything still works without it.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LOBBYING_NO_REQUIREMENT", "An option you mark as lobbying names the existing requirement it seeks enforced or restored: a standard, or a determined matter of the plan. Lobbying for anything else is not an act this record holds. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LOOK_AGAIN_REFUSED", "A day to look at the plan again is written year-month-day. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ADD_OPTION", "An option in a plan is a member's act: adding one, revising one or adopting a proposal. An assistant may propose options; a member adopts them. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CLOSE_PLAN", "Closing a plan is a member's act, with a reason. A plan never closes itself. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CONFIRM", "Confirming, correcting or disputing a local fact (a holiday calendar, an office's hours, the time zone), and confirming a rule your team drafted, is a member's act. An assistant may re-check a source and report what it found; it may not record a confirmation. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DECLARE_STANDARD", "Recording a standard is a member's act. An assistant may propose one for members to consider; it may not enter one in the record. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DISPOSE", "Choosing, declining or marking an option done or blocked is a member's decision. An assistant may not make it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_FILE_DOCKET", "Only a member, signed in as themselves, files to a case's docket. A machine, the assistant or an operator token cannot. Nothing was filed.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_JUDGE", "Whether a checkpoint's condition was met is the team's own judgment. An assistant may not make it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_MARK", "Only a member, acting for themselves, can mark a result from a paid or account-gated service; no machine, scheduled task or unattended process can. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_MARK_DOCKET_PRESSURE", "Only a member, signed in as themselves, marks a docket entry as a threat. Nothing was marked.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_PLACE_DOCKET", "Only the case's manager, signed in as themselves, places, declines or signs a public docket entry. A machine, the assistant or an operator token cannot. Nothing was published.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_PLAN", "An action plan is the team's own working material, and only a member opens it, changes what it is about, sets a scenario aside or restores it, pauses, resumes or closes it. An assistant may propose options; it may not do this. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_REGISTER_KEY", "A member registers their own signing key, from their own signed-in session. The credential that asked here has no member behind it: it is an automated one, the operator's token, or a call with nobody signed in. Sign in as yourself to register your key, or ask an administrator to register one for you. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_REQUEST_RECORDS", "Asking an office for its records, and recording what it answered, is a member's own act. This was not made by a member, so nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SCHEDULE", "Laying options out over time is a member's act. An assistant may propose options; it may not set a scenario. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_FREQUENCY", "How often an address is checked is set by a named member, with the member's reason. An assistant or a machine may suggest it; it may not set it. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_HOLD", "Saying whether a litigation hold is in place is a member's judgment, and somebody answers for it. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot say. Sign in to record it yourself.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_PASSWORD", "A member changes their own password, from their own signed-in session. The credential that asked here has no member behind it: it is an automated one, the operator's token, or a call with nobody signed in. Sign in as yourself to change your password. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_WORK_KIND", "A project's kinds of work are set by an owner of the project. An automated credential cannot set them. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_START", "Starting an option creates an action the team takes in the world, and only a member does that. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_WRITE_PLAN", "An action plan's record is written by members' acts only. An automated credential cannot write it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MEMBER_CAPTURE_ONLY", "This page is a private person's own site, or sits on a platform that asks for a login, and such a page is captured only by a member, in their own browser, as their own act. Your team's Civicsmith does not fetch it unattended or sign in to it, so nothing was fetched; a member who wants it captures it themselves.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MILESTONE_BAD_DATE", "A milestone's date is a calendar day, written as year, month and day. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MILESTONE_ITEM_UNKNOWN", "There is no question or step of this project by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MILESTONE_NO_NAME", "Give the milestone a name, in at most 200 characters. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MILESTONE_WAITS_ON_NOTHING", "A milestone waits on at least one question the project draws on or one step its participants can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_ATTESTED_BY_DOCUMENT", "The event named for this document is not one the document attests, so its date cannot be the date of this step. Name an event the document attests, or none. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_DISPOSITION", "Setting something down means deferring it (set aside for now) or dismissing it (declined); taking it up is a different act. Choose deferred or dismissed. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_SOURCE_OWNER", "The frequency of an address is set by an owner of a project that holds a monitored document there, and you own none of them. Ask an owner of one of those projects. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_CONCERNED", "The record does not show this document concerning the subject this instance follows, so it cannot be placed in it or excuse one of its steps. Resolve the document to the subject first, or use it in the instance of the subject it does concern. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_HELD_FROM_SOURCE", "This standard is already seen by every member of your team, so there is nothing to release. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_YOUR_CAPTURE", "Only the member who captured a result can mark it as from their own account on a paid service. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_YOUR_CEILING", "Nothing was changed, because a member's daily limit on the assistant is theirs alone to set or look at.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_BUNDLE", "This did not say which document it is about, so nothing was done.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_CAPTURE", "A step is filled by a captured document, named by its fingerprint, and this request names none. Name the document. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_CARDINALITY", "One step does not say how many documents it may hold (exactly one, at most one, or any number), so the record could not tell a step holding too many from one holding the usual set. Say how many. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_DECIDER", "A decision is recorded under the member who took it, and this request reached the record without one. Sign in and decide again. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_DEFINITION_VERSION", "Setting aside one of the record's own questions is a decision about the way a body is said to work — and that description is written down, dated, and rewritten when the team learns better. This request does not say which of those versions you were reading when you decided, so the record cannot say what you actually judged. Open the question again and send the version shown beside it. Nothing was recorded.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_EVIDENCE", "What is recorded about a source is recorded with its evidence. Name the evidence. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_MEMBER_BEHIND_CALLER", "the caller is a machine credential, so there is no participation to check", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PLACEMENTS", "Threading places documents at the steps of a flow, and this request places none. Name at least one step and the document that fills it. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_QUESTION", "A standing question needs its words, and none were given. Nothing was read or changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SERVICE", "A result from a paid or account-gated service names the service it came from. Name it. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SIGHT_LIST", "A detail about a source that is stored can be read only by the members listed for it, and none is listed. List at least one member, or record that the detail is known without storing it. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_STAGE", "This request does not say which step of the flow it is about. Name the step. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_STAGES", "A declared flow is its steps in order, and this one names no step. Name at least one step. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_STAGE_KEY", "One step of this flow has no key, so nothing could later be placed at it or found missing from it. Give every step a key. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_ADDRESS", "No monitored document you can see is checked at that address, so there is no check whose frequency could be set there. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CAPTURE", "No capture the record holds answers to that digest. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CLAIM", "There is no claim here by that number that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_DOCKET_ENTRY", "There is no docket entry here by that name for you: it does not exist, or it belongs to a case you do not see. Nothing was written.", note="docket's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_FACT", "No local fact of the active jurisdiction profiles answers to that path. A path names one profile's holiday year (of its office calendar or of a named closure list), an office's hours or the time zone. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_FORCE", "No confirmed force of a provision answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_GUIDE", "No reading guide you can see answers to that id. Nothing was written.", note="reading-guides' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_INQUIRY", "No question answers to that id here. One you may not see is answered exactly as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_INTERVIEW", "There is no interview of this project by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_MILESTONE", "There is no milestone here by that number that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_OPTION", "The plan holds no option of that id; the first one not found is named. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PLAN", "No action plan answers to that id here. A plan in a project you may not see is answered exactly as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PLANNING_PROPOSAL", "There is no planning proposal here by that number that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PLAN_PROPOSAL", "No proposal for an option answers to that id in a plan you may see. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PROGRESSION", "No flow of that key has been declared, so there is nothing to place documents in or to decide about. Declare the flow first. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_RECORD", "No record of a version known in force through a date answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_RECORDS_REQUEST", "No records request you can see answers to that id. One about a policy you may not see is answered exactly as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_SOURCE", "No source you can see answers to that id. Nothing was written.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_STANDARD", "No standard answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_DETAIL_TOO_LONG", "An option's detail is at most 5,000 characters. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_KEY_REFUSED", "A plan holds no cost, budget, money to be spent, assignee, hours or significance score. Those are not what this record is for. Send the act without them. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_NOT_CHOSEN", "Only an option the team has chosen is started. Choose it first. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_NO_SUBJECT", "An option serves at least one of the plan's matters, and names only matters the plan is about. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_NO_SUMMARY", "An option needs a summary of 1 to 200 characters. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OPTION_STARTED", "That option has already been started; the action it created is named. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ORIGIN_NOT_A_DOCUMENT", "Only a captured document came from a system, and this is not one: a question, a project or an action was written in the record. Nothing was recorded.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ORIGIN_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Saying which system a document came from is a statement a named member makes and is named beside, and this came from an automated credential or from nobody. Sign in and make it yourself. Nothing was recorded.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ORIGIN_NO_SYSTEM", "This did not name the system the document came from, or named it at more than 200 characters. Name it briefly and try again. Nothing was recorded.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OVERRIDE_INVALID", "An override names the held standard and portion it displaces, and until when: a recorded event or a later revision of this standard. The answer names the field not in that form. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PARTICIPANT", "the account has joined the project this run is over", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PHASE_CYCLE", "A phase cannot start after itself: following when each phase starts leads back to the phase named. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PHASE_MALFORMED", "A phase has an id, a name, the chosen options it holds, when it starts (at the plan's start, after another phase, on one outcome of another phase's checkpoint, when another matter's track reaches a point, or when an obligation's occurrence reaches a state: met, met late, overdue or undetermined), and may have a checkpoint after 1 to 3,650 days, a condition of up to 500 characters and the phase each judgment leads to. The phase named was not so. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PHASE_OPTION_NOT_CHOSEN", "A phase holds only options the team has chosen. Choose the option first. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_BAD_FORM", "A proposal is taken up as proposed, taken up with your own wording, or set aside for your own. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_BAD_KIND", "A planning proposal is a question or a step. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_BY_ACT_ONLY", "An action plan changes only through its own acts, so its history and what is read from it never disagree. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_CLOSED", "This plan has been closed. A closed plan stays readable, and nothing is added to it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_DECIDED", "This proposal was already taken up or set aside. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_HISTORY_REWRITTEN", "An action plan's history is never edited; each act adds to it. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NOT_A_MACHINE", "A member writes a question or a step themselves; a proposal is the assistant's, drawn from her words. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NOT_OF_PROJECT", "A planning run works on a plan of the project it is opened over, and this plan is another project's. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NOT_YOUR_RUN", "The assistant proposes only for a run it holds, and this credential holds no such run. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NO_REASON", "This act needs a reason in your own words, of 1 to 500 characters, with no quotation mark, backslash or line break. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NO_SUBJECT", "A plan is about 1 to 50 matters: an open question, or one standard's outcome of a determination. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NO_TEXT", "Say what the question or step is, in at most 500 characters. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_NO_TITLE", "A plan needs a title of 1 to 200 characters, with no quotation mark, backslash or line break. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE", "An action plan reads matters, actions and runs held by other parts of the record, and one of them is not in your team's Civicsmith yet, so the plan is not answered in part. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PORTION_UNKNOWN", "The portion named is not a portion recorded for that standard. Name the portion as it was recorded, or none. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PRESSURE_MARKED", "That entry is already marked as pressure, and a mark is never rewritten. Nothing was written.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PRESSURE_NO_ENTRY", "The entry is named by its position in the action's correspondence, counted from zero, and no entry stands at the position given. Nothing was written.", note="action-holds' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROGRESSION_NO_LABEL", "A declared flow carries a name a person can read, and this one has none. Give it a name. Nothing was written.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROGRESSION_VERSION_NOT_HELD", "The record holds no such version of this flow. The versions it does hold are named beside this message, and each reads back in full.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_NOT_WATCHED", "No member chose to keep watching this project's sources, so nothing that arrives reopens its work. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_ADOPTED", "That proposal has already been adopted as an option, which is named. A proposal is adopted once. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_BOUND_REACHED", "That planning run has made every proposal it was allowed. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_PROPOSER", "A proposal names who made it. This one came with no signed-in caller. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_RUN", "An assistant's proposal names the planning run it was made under, one you can see. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_SOURCE", "An assistant's proposal names what it rests on: findings, determinations, standards, consequences, plans or options you can see. One named is none of those here; one you may not see is answered as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_RUN_NOT_RUNNING", "That planning run is no longer running, so it proposes nothing more. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_RUN_OTHER_PLAN", "That run is not a planning run of this plan. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_WHY_REFUSED", "A proposal says why it is offered, in 1 to 500 characters. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVENANCE_REGISTER_REFUSED", "This document's account of where it came from breaks rules that the version it revises did not break, so nothing was written. Each broken rule is listed beside this message. Correct the account and save the document again.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUESTION_NOT_HELD", "The question named is not one your team's record holds that you may see. Name one, or none. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUIET_NOT_QUIET", "The work on this project has not gone quiet: a step is still open, or something is still awaited. Nothing was written.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REAUTH_DUE", "Type your password again to do this. Signing or publishing a case, changing administrators and connecting Claude always ask for it. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECEIPT_MALFORMED", "A receipt names the captured document's fingerprint, the address it was fetched from and when, and one of those was missing or not in its form, so no receipt was signed.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECEIPT_NO_KEY", "Your team's Civicsmith holds no key to sign its receipts with, so this receipt was not signed, and nothing claims that it was. Whoever hosts your team's Civicsmith can add one.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_ANSWER_NO_CAPTURE", "An answer saying the office produced the policy names the captured document it produced, one the record holds and you can see. None was named, or the one named is not held, so nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_ANSWER_NO_GROUND", "An answer saying the office withheld the policy records the ground it gave, in at most 1,000 characters. None was given, so nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_ANSWER_UNKNOWN", "The answer to a records request is one of four: produced (the office produced the text), none_exists (it says no such record exists), withheld (it declined, and why) or no_answer (none came). This was none of them, so nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_REQUEST_ANSWERED", "This records request already holds its answer, and an answer is never replaced. Nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_REQUEST_NOT_CITED", "A records request is opened for a policy the record knows only because something it holds cites it. This one is held another way, so nothing was written.", note="capture-requests' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECOVERY_CODES_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Recovery codes are given to an active member, for their own account, from their own signed-in session. Nothing was issued.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REGISTER_BYTES_UNSTATED", "Each document this save registers must state its size, as a whole number of bytes, and one of them states none, or a size no document can have. The record keeps each document's size so it can later check that the stored copy is whole. Nothing was written. State the document's size in bytes and save again.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RELEASE_NOT_OWNER", "A policy that is not public is released by an owner of the project its source material is filed in. You are not one. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REPORT_BAD_SINCE", "Say from when the report runs, as an instant, no later than now. Nothing was kept.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REPORT_NO_TEXT", "A status report holds your words, in at most 20,000 characters. Nothing was kept.", note="investigation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RESET_LINK_DEAD", "This password reset link does not work any more: it was used, it expired, or a newer one was made. Nothing was changed. Ask an administrator for a new link.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RESET_LINK_MEMBER_NOT_ACTIVE", "A password reset link is made only for an active member of your team. Nothing was made.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RULE_NOT_CONFIRMED", "Only a rule your team confirmed and still applies can be offered to the shared profile. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RULE_NO_REASON", "Say why, in at most 500 characters. None was given, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="local-facts' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SCENARIO_NAME_REFUSED", "A scenario needs a name of 1 to 200 characters, with no quotation mark, backslash or line break. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SECRET_NOT_RECOGNISED", "That secret was not recognized, so nothing was recorded. Check it and try again.", note="sources' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SECURITY_COUNTS_UNREADABLE", "The security counts could not be read just now, so none were given: they are missing, not zero. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SECURITY_KIND_UNKNOWN", "That is not a kind of refused request the security count keeps, so nothing was counted. This is a fault in how your team's Civicsmith was built, not in the record.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SECURITY_PERIOD_INVALID", "The security map shows a period of up to 90 days within the last 90, from an earlier time to a later one. The period asked was not one of those. Nothing was changed. Choose another period.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SESSION_LOCKED", "This page locked after a while without use. Type your password to carry on where you were, or sign out. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGNER_KEY_HELD_BY_ANOTHER", "This key is registered to another member, so it cannot be yours. Make a new key in this browser. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGNER_KEY_REVOKED", "This key was revoked, so it cannot be registered again. Make a new key in this browser, or ask an administrator. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGNER_MEMBER_NOT_ACTIVE", "That member’s membership is not active, so your team's Civicsmith would refuse anything signed with their key. Nothing was written. Reinstate the member first if they should be able to sign again.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGNER_MEMBER_NOT_ENROLLED", "That person has not enrolled yet. A signing key belongs to a member who has taken up their invitation and chosen a handle; until then your team's Civicsmith would refuse anything signed with it, so registering it now would put a key on the roster that cannot sign. Nothing was written. Send them their invitation link, and register the key once they have enrolled.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_ACT_INVALID", "The government act a proposal names is given by its id, in at most 200 characters, and this one is not. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_ALREADY_SUPERSEDED", "The standard named is already superseded by another, which the answer names. A standard is superseded once; supersede the later one instead. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_CITED_BY_MISSING", "A standard known only because a document cites it is recorded with where it is cited: the captured document and the passage that cites it. None was given, or it is not held. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_DATE_INVALID", "The date asked about is written YYYY-MM-DD, and this one is not. Nothing was answered.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_FIELD_INVALID", "A field of this act (where the standard sits in its law, how much of it is held, its family, designation or edition, or when an adoption took effect) is not in the form it takes. The answer names the field. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_FIELD_UNKNOWN", "This act takes only the fields it names, and the ones listed are not among them. The record holds a standard's citation, kind, issuer, text, period and reason, and never a view of its merit. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_KIND_UNKNOWN", "A standard is a statute, a regulation, an ordinance, a court decision or order, an adopted policy, a public commitment, or a documented standard set by a standards body, a profession, a regulator or an accreditor. This one names none of them. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_CITE", "A standard is recorded with its citation: how it is cited, in at most 200 characters. None was given, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_ID", "A standard is read by its id, and none was named. Name the standard to read. Nothing was answered.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_ISSUER", "A standard names the body that made it. None was given. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_REASON", "A standard is recorded with your reason: in your own words, why the team holds its government to it, in at most 2,000 characters. None was given, or it is not words, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL", "No proposal of a standard answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NO_TEXT", "A standard is held with its own words as captured: name at least one passage of a captured document that holds its text. None was named. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_PERIOD_INVALID", "A standard's period in force is a start and an end, each a date written YYYY-MM-DD or left unstated, and the end is not before the start. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_PORTION_NOT_IN_TEXT", "A portion of a standard is one of the passages recorded as its own words. The passage named is not one of them. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_PROPOSAL_ADOPTED", "This proposal was already adopted, as the standard the answer names. A proposal is adopted once. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_PROPOSER_UNNAMED", "This proposal carries nobody. A proposal is labeled with who made it, and one nobody can be named for could say nothing. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_SEARCH_MISSING", "A standard looked for and not found is recorded with the searches made: the portals, sites or offices searched, and any records request and its reply. None was given, or one is not in that form. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_SUPERSEDES_UNKNOWN", "The standard this one is said to supersede is not held in the record. Name one that is. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_TEXT_NOT_HELD_AS", "A standard recorded as cited, or as looked for and not found, holds none of its own words, so no passage is named as its text. Record it as held with its text instead, or name no text. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_TEXT_UNRESOLVED", "A passage named as this standard's text is not held in the record. Capture the document and cite the passage first. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_WHY_INVALID", "A proposal says why the standard applies, in at most 240 characters. None was given, or it is too long. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_WRITTEN_ELSEWHERE", "A standard enters the record only when a member records or adopts one, and it is never edited: a correction is a new standard that supersedes it. This write is neither. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDING_SWITCH_OFF", "Standing questions are switched off for the Claude account that would answer this one, so the assistant did not look. Whoever holds that account can switch standing questions on. Nothing was read or changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUBJECT_IN_ACTIVE_PLAN", "That matter is already in an open plan of this project, which is named. A matter is in one open plan of a project at a time; work in that one, or close it first. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUBJECT_NOT_LIVE", "That matter is no longer live: the determination has been superseded, or the question is closed. Plan from the live one. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUBJECT_NOT_OF_PROJECT", "A plan is about the project's own matters: a question the project draws on, or a determination the project made. This one belongs to another project. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SURFACE_BOUND_REACHED", "This investigation has already opened as many questions as the member who started it allowed. Nothing was created. The investigation ends at its next step and says which limit stopped it.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SURFACE_NO_BOUND", "This investigation was not given a limit on how many questions it may open, so it may open none: an assistant opening questions without a limit fills the record with questions nobody asked for. The limit is set by the member who starts the investigation. Nothing was created.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SURFACE_NO_RUN", "An assistant opens a question only inside an investigation it is running, and this one named none that can be read here. The investigation is what records the lens and the purpose the question was opened under, so without one nothing could say why it exists. Nothing was created.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SURFACE_RUN_NOT_RUNNING", "The investigation this question was to be opened inside has ended. A question is read against the conditions of the investigation that opened it, and those stopped being current when it stopped. Nothing was created; a member can start a new investigation.", note="run-rules' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TARGET_INVALID", "A target names what is measured and the passage stating it, a threshold (at least, at most or within, an exact number and its unit), the period it applies to, and the body's definition of the measure or that none is stated. The answer names the field not in that form. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_AUTHORED_DROPPED", "This document is a member's own observation, and this revision no longer says so. Removing that would let a member's word read as a captured document. What the document is cannot be revised; to withdraw an observation, record a new one.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_AUTHORED_UNEARNED", "This document claims to be a member's own firsthand observation, but it did not come through the act that records one. Only that act can mark a document as an observation, because only that act takes the author from the signed-in account. Record the observation through it, or remove the claim.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_AUTHOR_SUPPLIED", "That request names who the author is. The record takes the author of an observation from the account that is signed in, never from the request — a request that names its own author could sign as somebody else. Send the observation without an author and it is recorded as yours.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_NOT_A_MEMBER", "A firsthand observation is a person saying what they saw, in their own name, and it stands on that person's trust. The credential that asked is an automated one, and it has no eyes to have seen anything with. Sign in and record it yourself.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_NO_WORDS", "The observation is empty. Write what you saw, in your own words; nothing is filled in for you.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_OBSERVED_AT_INVALID", "An observation needs the date you saw it, as a calendar date (for example 2026-09-10) or a date and time, and not a date later than now. The record keeps that date apart from the moment you wrote it down, because they are two different facts.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_ORIGIN_NOT_MEMBER", "This document is a member's own observation, and this revision of its record claims it came from somewhere else — a fetch, a sweep, or a machine. That would let a member's word pass for a captured publication. An observation's origin is the member who made it, and that cannot be revised.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_WORDS_REGISTERED", "The record already holds, under another document, the exact bytes this observation would be stored as — which can only happen if somebody registered them in advance. Nothing was recorded. Try again: the next attempt is stored under a new identifier and new bytes.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TESTIMONY_WORDS_TOO_LONG", "The observation is longer than one passage this record stores. Record it as more than one observation; each is kept exactly as written and each can be cited.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEXT_NOT_MEMBER_CAPTURED", "The text of a standard behind a paywall or in a reading room is held only from a capture a member made themselves. A passage named was captured another way. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NOT_A_MEMBER", "A theme is declared by a person, in their own name, and every reading of it shows whose lens it is. The credential that asked is an automated one, which has nobody behind it to hold the idea. Sign in and declare it yourself.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NOT_EVIDENCE", "That leg rests on a THEME. A theme is one member's declared lens — an idea they use to gather material — and it is never the basis of a claim, so nothing can rest on it or on a document's membership in it. Cite the document or the passage itself: what a finding rests on is content, whatever theme led you to it.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NOT_FOUND", "No theme is recorded under that id. Use the id the declaration returned, or list the themes to find it.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NO_NAME", "A theme needs its idea in a few words — what you are calling it, such as \"deferred maintenance\" — as well as its test. Nothing was declared.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NO_PROPOSER", "A proposal must say who proposed it, and this one arrived carrying nobody. The record stamps the proposer from the credential that asked; nothing was written.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_NO_TEST", "A theme needs its TEST: one sentence a document or a passage either passes or fails, so any member can check a placement against it. Without one the theme is a label anything could wear, and it cannot be declared.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_PLACEMENT_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Placing a document in a theme is a member's judgment that it passes the theme's test, recorded in their name. An automated credential may only PROPOSE a placement, which stays a hunch until a member confirms it. Sign in to place it, or propose it instead.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_REASON_TOO_LONG", "The note on this placement is longer than the record stores in one passage. It was refused rather than cut. Shorten it and try again.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_TARGET_NOT_FOUND", "Nothing you can see in the record answers to that document or passage id, so it cannot be placed in a theme. Name a document by its id, or a passage by the content id it was minted under.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_TOO_LONG", "The theme's name or its test is longer than the record stores in one passage. It was refused rather than cut, so nothing you wrote is silently lost. Shorten it and declare it again.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_WITHDRAW_NOTHING_STANDING", "Nothing stands in this theme at that document or passage: it was never placed or proposed there, or it has already been taken back. There is nothing to withdraw.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_WITHDRAW_NOT_A_MEMBER", "Taking a document or a passage out of a theme, or turning down a proposal, is a member's own judgment, done in their name. A machine may propose a placement; it cannot take one back.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_WITHDRAW_NOT_THE_PLACER", "A membership is taken back by the member who placed it, or by an administrator. Any member may turn down a proposal, but another member's placement stands on their judgment until they withdraw it.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEME_WITHDRAW_NO_REASON", "Say why. A placement taken back or a proposal turned down keeps its reason beside it, so the next reader of the theme can see what was judged and on what ground.", note="connections' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THROUGH_AFTER_CHECK", "A source shows a version in force only up to the day it was last retrieved, and the date given is later than that. Give that day or an earlier one, or capture the source again. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THROUGH_INVALID", "The date a version is known in force through is a day written YYYY-MM-DD, and not before the day the version came into force. This one is not. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THROUGH_NO_SOURCE", "A version known in force through a date is recorded with the passage of the source checked that day, a captured document you may see. None was named, or it is not held. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TIER_REFUSED", "A tier is stated only on a legal option, and is 1, 2, 3 or undetermined. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_AFTER", "One step here says it comes after a step this sequence does not contain, so the order cannot be worked out. Name a step that exists, or leave the ordering off and let it stand on its own.", note="progressions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_KEYED_SERVICE", "That is not an outside service this team can hold a key for. Nothing was changed.", note="credentials' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNSPLICEABLE_PLAN", "The plan's record cannot be extended in place. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_BASIS_INVALID", "A version read from two captures names two held captures of one address whose texts differ, and the version it supersedes. These are not that. Nothing was written.", note="standards' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_CHAIN_BAD_ANCHOR", "That is not the shape a capture identity has, so nothing was looked up. A capture is named by the sha256 of its bytes; this says the request was malformed rather than letting it read as a document the record does not hold.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_CHAIN_NO_ADDRESS", "That request did not say which document address to read the versions of. Versions are versions OF something, so it asks rather than answering for a document you did not name.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_CHAIN_NO_SUCH_VERSION", "The record holds no version of that document with those bytes. Rather than pick the closest-looking one and call it the version before this, it says so — naming the wrong predecessor is the defect this read was built to end.", note="provenance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.WATCH_END_REFUSED", "A watch ends on a calendar day, today or later, or has no end date. That day could not be used. Nothing was changed.", note="monitoring's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.WORK_KIND_UNKNOWN", "A project's kinds of work are drawn from: reporting, fixing, legal, oversight, other. Nothing was written.", note="action-plans' translation, keyed by its code")

